('112.27.b.9.C',3,'The ozone layer in Earth''s atmosphere helps life by...','["absorbing harmful ultraviolet radiation", "warming the oceans", "making rain", "creating oxygen"]'::jsonb,0,'UV can damage living cells.','original'),
('112.27.b.9.C',3,'Which gas makes up most of Earth''s atmosphere?','["oxygen", "nitrogen", "hydrogen", "carbon dioxide"]'::jsonb,1,'About 78% is nitrogen.','original'),
('112.27.b.9.C',4,'Why is the greenhouse effect important for life on Earth?','["it removes oxygen", "it blocks all sunlight", "it traps heat that keeps the planet warm enough", "it cools the planet"]'::jsonb,2,'Without it Earth would be far colder.','original'),
('112.27.b.9.C',4,'Venus is too hot for liquid water because it is...','["made of ice", "too small", "too far from the Sun", "close to the Sun and has a very thick carbon dioxide atmosphere"]'::jsonb,3,'Its atmosphere traps heat.','original'),
('112.27.b.9.C',4,'Mars is too cold for liquid water on the surface mainly because it...','["has a thin atmosphere and is farther from the Sun", "is closer to the Sun", "has no gravity", "has too much oxygen"]'::jsonb,0,'Little heat is retained.','original'),
